# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# POOJARO — environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in only what you need. The site runs
# end to end with none of it set: the datastore falls back to a local seeded
# JSON store, payment falls back to cash on delivery, and every feature that
# needs a credential says so plainly instead of pretending to work.
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored. Never commit real keys.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# === Site ==================================================================

# Absolute origin, used for canonical URLs, Open Graph images and the sitemap.
# Must be the real domain in production or share links will point at localhost.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# === Data backend ==========================================================

# "local" (default) keeps everything in a JSON file under .data/. Real cart,
# real orders, real stock deduction, real audit log — no credentials needed.
# "firestore" switches to the same schema the Flutter app uses.
DATA_BACKEND=local

# Where the local store writes. Ignored when DATA_BACKEND=firestore.
LOCAL_DATA_DIR=.data

# === Firebase (only when DATA_BACKEND=firestore) ============================
#
# Service account credentials from Firebase console → Project settings →
# Service accounts → Generate new private key. Requires `npm install firebase-admin`.
# FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY keeps its literal \n sequences; quote the whole value.

# FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=poojaro-xxxxx
# FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=firebase-adminsdk-xxxxx@poojaro-xxxxx.iam.gserviceaccount.com
# FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nMIIE...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"

# === Sessions ==============================================================
#
# HMAC key for signed admin and customer cookies. REQUIRED in production — the
# app refuses to boot without it rather than falling back to a shared default.
# Generate one:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"

# SESSION_SECRET=

# === First admin account ===================================================
#
# Seeded on first boot. ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD is REQUIRED in production so the
# panel is never created with a password that is in this file. Change it after
# the first login; it is only read when the account does not yet exist.

# ADMIN_SEED_EMAIL=owner@poojaro.in
# ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD=

# === Payments — Razorpay ===================================================
#
# Until these are set, checkout offers cash on delivery only and the online
# methods are shown as unavailable with a reason. Nothing is faked: an order is
# marked paid only after Razorpay's HMAC signature verifies against the secret.
#
# Dashboard → Settings → API Keys. The key id is public by design; the secret
# must stay server-side and must never be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_xxxxxxxxxxxx
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_xxxxxxxxxxxx
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=

# Dashboard → Settings → Webhooks. Point it at /api/payments/webhook and
# subscribe to payment.captured and payment.failed. Without this, a payment is
# lost if the shopper closes the tab before returning to the site.
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# === Store contact details =================================================
#
# These seed the Settings record on first boot; after that the admin panel is
# the source of truth and changing them here has no effect.
#
# Leave WHATSAPP_NUMBER blank and the floating support button hides itself
# rather than linking to a number nobody answers.

# SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@poojaro.in
# SUPPORT_PHONE=+91 98765 43210
# WHATSAPP_NUMBER=919876543210
# FREE_DELIVERY_THRESHOLD=499
# DELIVERY_FEE=49

# === Shipping serviceability (optional) ====================================
#
# Without these, delivery dates come from the offline India Post PIN prefix map
# plus the lead times in admin Settings, and are labelled estimates. With them,
# implement the provider branch in src/lib/domain/shipping.ts to get live
# courier serviceability and quoted ETAs.

# SHIPPING_PROVIDER=delhivery
# SHIPPING_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# === Outbound notifications (optional) =====================================
#
# In-app notifications always work — they are rows in our own datastore, shown
# in the account area and the admin panel. These add email, SMS and WhatsApp
# delivery of the same messages. Senders are stubbed: set the credentials, then
# implement the matching send* function in src/lib/domain/notifications.ts.

# EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend
# EMAIL_API_KEY=
# EMAIL_FROM=orders@poojaro.in

# Indian transactional SMS also needs a DLT-registered template.
# SMS_PROVIDER=msg91
# SMS_API_KEY=
# SMS_SENDER_ID=POOJRO

# WhatsApp Cloud API. Templates must be approved by Meta before they will send.
# WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
# WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=
